# Users of valkey-queue (specs/07 §5.3, NFR-SEC-03): each component reaches only its own keys and no
# administrative command. The @<NAME>_PASSWORD@ placeholders come from the environment
# (start-queue.sh); a phase that adds keys adds them here. Dramatiq names its namespace `dramatiq`
# as a key of its scripts, then `dramatiq:<queue>...`.
#
# default: the container health check only.
user default on nopass -@all +ping
# api: puts checks on the Dramatiq queues, keeps the queue positions, reads the event streams.
user api on >@API_PASSWORD@ ~dramatiq ~dramatiq:* ~queue:* %R~sub:* +@all -@dangerous
# worker: takes checks from the queues, removes their positions, holds leases and counts attempts,
# writes the events of its checks and their results (it reads neither stream).
user worker on >@WORKER_PASSWORD@ ~dramatiq ~dramatiq:* %W~queue:* ~lease:* ~attempts:* %W~sub:* %W~judge:results +@all -@dangerous
# ingest: reads the results through its consumer group, writes `finalized` to the event streams;
# its leader holds leader:ingest, and the watchdog looks whether a worker holds a check.
user ingest on >@INGEST_PASSWORD@ ~judge:results %W~sub:* ~leader:ingest %R~lease:* +@all -@dangerous
